target/
*.class
.env
logs/
.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Terraform state carries every value it managed, in plaintext - including admin passwords and
# client secrets. Never versioned. (deploy/pingfederate/terraform had its own ignore file; the
# gm-api tree had none, which is the shape of leak this repo has already had once.)
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Key material of any kind. Belt and braces: build.yml fails the build if one is ever tracked.
*.jwk
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.lic

# PF config archives. A configArchive is a plain zip that CONTAINS pf.jwk, the system keys, both
# keystores, the admin password hash and master-key-reversible client secrets - so committing one
# publishes the master key. data.staging.zip reached a public remote exactly this way.
#
# This pattern lives at the ROOT deliberately. Until now the only thing stopping it was
# deploy/pingfederate/.gitignore, so the protection travelled with that directory: moving the build
# context out of deploy/ silently un-ignored the archives sitting beside it, and the very next
# `git add -A` staged data.staging.zip again. Ignore rules for a repo-wide invariant do not belong
# in a subdirectory that can be moved.
data*.zip

# Editor / tool droppings
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.claude/worktrees/
dependency-reduced-pom.xml

# Generated by the build and published by CI, never tracked (plan decision 18, 2026-09-27): a reactor-wide file
# that every test or documentation change regenerated conflicted in Phase 0's parallel merges. The coverage dashboard
# is written by tools/coverage-report.py after `mvn verify`, the showcase's documents by
# tools/build-showcase-docs.mjs; a CI Build run whose reactor build completes publishes them as its
# coverage-dashboard and showcase artefacts.
docs/coverage-dashboard.md
docs/coverage-dashboard.html
showcase/docs.js
